    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1441">

                <pb facs="0943" n="827" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg827"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.52/440.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Spanish Ambassador to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Spanish Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-10-09">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 9, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary</hi>: I appeal to the kind services of
                    your excellency for the purpose of entreating that you will be good enough to
                    give the necessary orders, with all the despatch which the case requires, for a
                    United States warship to be sent to Mazatlan, if possible, for the protection of
                    Spanish subjects resident at that place.</p>
                <p>I am informed by telegraphic despatches just received, that these people are
                    being subjected to fresh acts of injustice at the hands of the Constitutionalist
                    forces, who have also arrested the Spanish Consular Agent at that port.</p>
                <p>Expressing, in anticipation, to your excellency my sincere thanks,</p>
                <p>I take [etc.].</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Juan Riaño</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
